								<div class="title" id="post-title-4550771">
																		Author Post
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/absentmindednihilist" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2812984); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2812984&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608217723" alt="AbsentmindedNihilist" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2812984)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/absentmindednihilist" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2812984); return false;" >AbsentmindedNihilist</a></span> <span class="odate time_1584374568 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">16 Mar 2020 16:02</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4550771">
									

<p>This is going to be the first tale in a series that should help expand upon the events that take place between 3240 and 4698, and provide more detail and depth to the Verdant, the Veldt, and their relationship. If anything in this tale or those skips interests you, or if you're a fan of some of my other mythology based skips (2547 and 2889 being the most prominent) please message me: I'm trying to build a canon and desperately need other authors.</p>
<p>This tale was spite-written in one sitting to prove to myself that I could, in fact, write, after receiving some frustrating feedback in a different creative class. It features many of my favorite things: grotesque and horrifying monsters, (hopefully) nuanced and original portrayals of mythological figures, and, of course, sapphic romance.</p>
<p>Big thanks to the following: Naepicfail, DrAkimoto, Mewltiverse, rimple, gerrymander, oboebandgeek, Scheals, and DrMoned.</p>
<p>Special shout outs to these wonderful folks: HammerMaiden for helping me get Set's voice down, MalyceGraves for helping me make the action sequences from barely coherent messes to something actually decent, Roget for doing an excellent in-depth review, and Tuomey for being supportive as hell and very handsome.</p>
<p>I tried very hard to make sure I recorded all of the people who critiqued this, but as always my episodic memory is barely functional, so if you remember reading a draft of this and aren't on the list, let me know + I'll add you.</p>

							</div>

								
